/*****************************************************************************
    jitSelfFn -- THE SHAPE THAT EXITED 139. A DRIVER WITH A PREAMBLE ABOVE A
    SELF-CALLING CALLEE, ITS GUARD RESET INSIDE THE DRIVER. 2026-08-05.

    ⚠ THIS IS incant/inlineSelfT's CRASHING HALF, PROMOTED FROM A BY-HAND
    RECIPE TO A RUNNABLE FIXTURE. inlineSelfT could only carry it as prose --
    rule H5, a fixture that dies takes every check below it with it -- and the
    reason it could not run was the defect S3 removes.

    THE DEFECT IT PINS. Emit-on-walk INLINES an ordinary callee into the
    caller's builder, so before S3 a self-call inside that inlined body had no
    separate function to name and got the ENCLOSING one:

        %selfcall = call i32 @jitFn0()      <- @jitFn0 IS THE DRIVER

    which re-enters the driver's ENTRY BLOCK and replays its whole preamble on
    every recursion. With the preamble harmless that is invisible; with the
    preamble holding the loop guard's reset, the guard is restored on every
    recursion and the recursion never ends.

    ⚠ SO THIS FIXTURE'S NEGATIVE CONTROL IS A HANG, NOT A RED, and the ladder
    must run it under a wall-clock cap for that reason (H5: a hang is not a
    wrong answer, it is the absence of a run, and it would silently delete every
    check below it). On a pre-S3 binary: exit 139 or no return, no degrade
    message, and no output after `jitRunAction: entering`.

    ⚠ WHY inlineSelfT's OWN GREEN HALF COULD NOT SEE IT, AND WHY displayForm
    COULD NOT EITHER: dfDrive's body is exactly ONE statement, so re-entering
    the whole function happened to equal re-entering the callee. Rung JC was
    green for a reason true of ITS DRIVER rather than of the mechanism -- the
    same class as `continue` appearing to work because both arms fell to the
    back edge. A driver with a preamble is the NORMAL case, and precisely the
    shape genParse's emitted rules will have.

    WHAT IS ASSERTED, and none of it is an absence check (rule H4):

      sfPre   = 1   THE PREAMBLE RAN EXACTLY ONCE. This is the load-bearing row
                    and it is the defect stated as a number: under the replay
                    the driver's preamble re-executes on every recursion, so
                    this reads 4, or the run never ends. ONE is the only value a
                    driver whose preamble ran as written can produce.
      sfCount = 4   THE NUMBER OF ACTIVATIONS. Non-zero on purpose -- a result
                    slot that merely defaults to zero cannot produce it, and it
                    is the sibling that stops sfPre's `1` from being a constant
                    the machinery would emit anyway.
      sfOut   = 3   THE OUTERMOST ACTIVATION'S LOCAL, read AFTER the recursive
                    call returns. Per-activation storage gives 3; aliased slots
                    give 0, because the innermost activation would have written
                    the shared slot last. Same discrimination J-R and jitJRL
                    use, one level further out.

    ⚠ NOTHING HERE READS A RETURNED VALUE, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE RATHER THAN
    INCIDENTAL: `return` under JIT has no emitter, it calls jitDegrade, so a row
    asserting what `sf(sfArg)` HANDED BACK would not be measuring this
    mechanism -- it would be asking a question that is not yet askable. The
    callee writes the globals itself; the driver only calls it. (Every green
    rung in the ladder asserts a FIELD's value after the action rather than a
    returned one, for exactly this reason.)

    ⚠⚠ ONE ROW IS PINNED WRONG ON PURPOSE, WITH ITS CAUSE MEASURED (H7's other
    half -- where a construct is built but not certified, pin it red rather than
    let an accident of topology imply coverage).

    `print "PREAMBLE":;` in the driver emits ONE LINE, which is what this
    fixture certifies -- one line is the observable form of "the preamble ran
    once", and under the replay it is not one. But THE LINE'S CONTENT IS WRONG:
    a jitted print of a bare string literal emits the string's LENGTH instead of
    its text.

        print "AB":;                jitted 2    oracle AB
        print "PREAMBLEPREAMBLE":;  jitted 16   oracle PREAMBLEPREAMBLE

    ⚠ PRE-EXISTING AND NOT S3's, AND THAT IS MEASURED RATHER THAN ARGUED: the
    identical 2 / 16 come out of a binary built from 6323adb -- before S1, S3
    and S4 existed -- rebuilt for the purpose and then reverted. It involves no
    self-call, no recursion and no inlining, so it is not this arc's to fix; it
    is the 2026-08-05 "recorded, not chased" print oddity with a sharper
    signature than the one recorded (silence was the earlier symptom; a number
    wearing the shape of data is the current one, which is the same escalation
    the corpus already names -- a conflated channel gets MORE dangerous as the
    system gets better). Degrade count is 0 throughout, so the wrong content is
    SILENT.

    ONE testing(), THEN NOTHING ELSE FIRES IT -- a second testing() on one
    action is the sequential-state-corruption tar baby, and the rung shape makes
    that unconstructable rather than merely avoided.

    ⚠ THE JITTED HALF RUNS FIRST AND THAT ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING. `testing()`
    routes to jitRunAction only `if input.isCoded` (Commands.rtn:663), and an
    interpreted run consumes that -- so an oracle placed above the jitted half
    silently sends it to jitRunIfTest instead, and the fixture measures the
    wrong engine at exit 0. Found the expensive way while writing this file.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT, and exactly ONE stop() in this file (rule H2): a
    second stop() anywhere above it silently deletes everything between.
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(SelfFn);
define
    sfDepth;
    sfArg;
    sfOut;
    sfCount;
    sfPre;
    /*  THE CALLEE. It mentions its own name, so an inlined copy of it calling
        itself is the discovery S3's map is populated by. sfLoc is a LOCAL --
        first named inside the body, so aCTionNamE stamps it isLocal -- and it
        is read AFTER the recursive call returns, which is what makes sfOut a
        statement about per-activation storage rather than about arithmetic.  */
    sf code={
        sfLoc = sfDepth;
        if sfDepth > 0;
            sfDepth = sfDepth - 1;
            sf(argument);
        sfCount = sfCount + 1;
        sfOut = sfLoc;
        };
    /*  ⚠ THE DRIVER'S PREAMBLE IS THE WHOLE FIXTURE. Three statements above the
        call, and the first of them is the loop guard's reset -- the exact
        placement inlineSelfT identified as the discriminating variable:
            guard reset OUTSIDE the driver -> nothing harmful replays -> exit 0
            guard reset INSIDE  the driver -> the reset replays forever -> 139
        Only the location of one statement differed there. Here it is inside.
        The driver does NOT assign the call's result -- see the return note in
        the header.  */
    sfDrive code={
        sfDepth = 3;
        sfPre = sfPre + 1;
        print "PREAMBLE":;
        sf(sfArg);
        };
    ;

sfArg   = 7;
sfCount = 0;
sfPre   = 0;
/*  ⚠ sfOut IS INITIALISED, AND IT HAS TO BE. A field that has never been given
    a value has no datA type, so it prints as its own TAG -- and the jitted store
    writes the baked gCount slot without stamping one, so the field stays
    tagless and the row reads `sfOut` instead of a number. That is the fixture's
    job to get right, not the engine's; 0 here makes 3 a real move rather than a
    value the default could also produce.  */
sfOut   = 0;

print "== SF PREAMBLE OUTPUT BEGINS ==":;
testing(sfDrive);
print "== SF PREAMBLE OUTPUT ENDS ==":;

print "SF jitted : pre = " sfPre " count = " sfCount " out = " sfOut:;

print "jitSelfFn SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
